Notebook[{
Cell["Unit 3 \[CenterDot] Attention, Part by Part", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"ad03dfdf-bb8c-4bae-90ce-0de7aa04f422"],

Cell["\<\
The transformer built from plain arrays and from primitive layers (Vaswani et \
al., 2017) \[LongDash] TensorNets units of learning, 3 of 4\
\>", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"1f2396d0-9dc4-45b4-b4f7-849d21cd9a32"],

Cell["\[Copyright] 2026 Computational Classnotes \[CenterDot] CC BY-NC-SA \
4.0", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7f7a7cea-a203-4d9e-b311-264c1488bba0"],

Cell["\<\
The transformer drops recurrence. Every word looks at every other word at \
once, through attention, and position is added as a code. This unit builds \
each part twice: from plain arrays, to see the mathematics, and as a Wolfram \
net from primitive layers, to train it. Each section checks that the two \
agree. Evaluate from top to bottom; it takes about a minute. The write-up \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Unit 3 \[CenterDot] Attention, Part by Part\
\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] has the same section numbers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b8d6bde6-d0ec-4aec-aa78-ab7739107938"],

Cell["Before you start: choose Evaluation \[RightPointer] Quit Kernel \
\[RightPointer] Local.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7e92c2ec-2c31-4e62-820c-\
f57a3773a03c"],

Cell["1. Toolkit", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"3b350e06-8582-45ed-a436-aa83c06a776a"],

Cell["\<\
Arrays first: softmaxRows, sdpa (scaled dot-product attention, \[Section]3), \
the masks (\[Section]5), mha (\[Section]6), pe (\[Section]7), ffn and \
layerNorm (\[Section]8), encoderLayer and decoderLayer (\[Section]9). Then \
the same parts as nets built from primitive layers: mhaNet, peNet, ffnNet, \
encoderLayerNet, decoderLayerNet. The array versions read their weights out \
of the nets, so the two can be compared exactly. Last, the training and \
decoding recipes: smoothTarget (\[Section]11), warmRate (\[Section]12), \
lengthPenalty (\[Section]13) and the parameter counts (\[Section]14).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"cc3643c8-7042-4af4-a784-dfe9f7dc27d4"],

