Cell["2. The idea: attention instead of recurrence", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"171cec3f-6be9-45bb-9ea7-bc2c3e9e3ea6"],

Cell["\<\
An LSTM (Unit 1) reads one word after another, so the first word reaches the \
last only through every step between them, and the steps cannot run in \
parallel. The transformer lets every position look at every other position \
directly. Each position asks a question (its query), every position offers an \
answer key and a value, and the output is an average of the values weighted \
by how well the keys match the query. Order is added as a position code.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d30f142d-17c6-492c-adfd-7c75b84cccaa"],

Cell["\<\
The paper\[CloseCurlyQuote]s model is an encoder\[Dash]decoder like Unit 1\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s, with each LSTM replaced by a stack of layers built from \
attention and a small feed-forward network:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fd88d8ab-c367-4da1-8b3f-6e22d0fccd27"],

