Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Fig. 1. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11]],
 "The transformer. Each encoder layer is self-attention then a feed-forward \
network, each wrapped as add & LayerNorm. Each decoder layer adds masked \
self-attention and attention over the encoder\[CloseCurlyQuote]s output \
(orange arrow). The paper uses N = 6."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b5f4241f-12ee-4611-a550-a558c00e7753"],

Cell["3. Scaled dot-product attention", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1b6c5802-f13a-4cf4-9fd3-10ec457c395b"],

Cell["\<\
Stack the queries as rows of Q, the keys as rows of K and the values as rows \
of V. Compare every query with every key by a dot product, divide by \[Sqrt]d\
\:2096 (\[Section]4), take the softmax of each row and average the values \
with those weights (Section 3.2.1 of the paper):\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"584979f8-391f-404a-997a-b11c16a21123"],

Cell["Attention(Q, K, V) = softmax( Q K\:1d40 / \[Sqrt]d\:2096 ) V", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"eaa73b88-63e8-47c7-8f6b-3ed9a5588793"],

Cell["3.1 Worked by hand: one query, two keys", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"a52f63bf-a531-414b-b989-b4179dc32164"],

Cell["\<\
Let q = (1, 0), with keys k\:2081 = (1, 0), k\:2082 = (0, 1) and values v\
\:2081 = (1, 0), v\:2082 = (0, 1); d\:2096 = 2. The scores are q\[CenterDot]k\
\:2081/\[Sqrt]2 = 0.7071 and q\[CenterDot]k\:2082/\[Sqrt]2 = 0. The softmax \
weights are e^0.7071/(e^0.7071 + 1) = 2.028/3.028 = 0.670 and 1/3.028 = \
0.330. The output is 0.670 v\:2081 + 0.330 v\:2082 = (0.670, 0.330): mostly \
the value of the matching key.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"2d4227df-fe59-4198-9bb3-2b2e42904939"],

