 CellLabel->"Out[4]=",ExpressionUUID->"32678620-0856-453e-9ed3-265d240ab9af"],

Cell["\<\
Check: {True, True}. The formula coded from arrays equals Wolfram\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s AttentionLayer with \"ScoreRescaling\" -> \"DimensionSqrt\
\" (4 queries, 7 keys), and every row of weights sums to 1.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"82b7f41c-1496-40c7-9ffb-2097fde79f76"],

Cell["4. Why divide by \[Sqrt]d\:2096", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"c064cea4-5210-41e3-bca5-e2dace687ab9"],

Cell["\<\
If the components of q and k are independent with mean 0 and variance 1, \
their dot product has mean 0 and variance d\:2096 (footnote 4 of the paper). \
For d\:2096 = 64 the scores are then about \[PlusMinus]8, the softmax is \
close to one-hot, and its gradient is tiny. Dividing by \[Sqrt]d\:2096 brings \
the variance back to 1.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"c57c2959-15c7-4096-b70c-bf7df3406cd1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "q\[CenterDot]k = q\:2081k\:2081 + \[Ellipsis] + ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["q", "d"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fd1b6ed8-232b-482d-9024-b7b4f671120e"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  SubscriptBox["k", "d"]],ExpressionUUID->
  "285135de-25cb-4575-8442-80711e70a5ff"],
 " is a sum of d\:2096 independent terms, each with mean 0 and variance E[q\
\.b2]E[k\.b2] = 1. Variances of independent terms add, so Var(q\[CenterDot]k) \
= d\:2096, and Var(q\[CenterDot]k/\[Sqrt]d\:2096) = d\:2096/d\:2096 = 1."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"966fdd3a-2335-4bd1-b5e4-1a87d7f8eb40"],

