Cell["Check: {True, True} for d\:2096 = 64.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"bfc2c341-c1f0-4955-a879-623ceed4e69f"],

Cell["5. Masks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"1a81cf5e-582a-4217-a1c3-7aa7c4d9c18b"],

Cell["\<\
A mask is added to the scores before the softmax: 0 where attention is \
allowed, a very large negative number where it is not, so those weights \
become 0. A padding mask hides padding at the end of short sequences. A \
causal mask stops position i of the decoder from seeing positions after i, so \
it cannot read the word it must predict (Section 3.2.3).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"517c29ab-8c58-4ab2-86a5-f6d7b48c83bf"],

Cell["\<\
For three positions the causal mask is ((0, \[Minus]\[Infinity], \[Minus]\
\[Infinity]), (0, 0, \[Minus]\[Infinity]), (0, 0, 0)). Row 1 can see only \
position 1, so its weights are (1, 0, 0) whatever the scores. Row 2 shares \
its weight between positions 1 and 2; row 3 sees all three.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"57fa80de-caf3-4b69-876a-216b17b48eca"],

