Cell["\<\
Check: {True, True}: ffnNet equals the formula at every position, and \
NormalizationLayer equals LayerNorm from arrays with a random \[Gamma] and \
\[Beta]. The paper normalises after the residual sum (post-norm); many later \
transformers normalise before the sub-layer (pre-norm), which is easier to \
train when there are many layers.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"48d78d4c-5db5-4b88-b9dc-6789be40eb82"],

Cell["9. One encoder layer and one decoder layer", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a8de0d6b-2381-48b4-8ac0-4781e0a3c64e"],

Cell["\<\
An encoder layer is self-attention, then the feed-forward network, each \
wrapped as LayerNorm(x + Sublayer(x)). A decoder layer has three sub-layers: \
causal self-attention over the output so far, attention over the encoder\
\[CloseCurlyQuote]s output (queries from the decoder, keys and values from \
the encoder) and the feed-forward network (Fig. 1).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4ef176f-351b-48e1-a8c9-ebd54ca25cf7"],

