 RowBox[{"{", 
  RowBox[{"True", ",", "180"}], "}"}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[17]=",ExpressionUUID->"c3c899c4-a369-4d72-b3b0-aa6faddadcb2"],

Cell["\<\
Check: {True, 180}: the embedding and the output projection are one array, \
stored once: 20 \[Times] 8 = 160 shared weights and 20 output biases.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8c702198-15e6-430e-ae10-f108b019a5ad"],

Cell["11. Label smoothing", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"ac70d55c-a7ae-408f-b6b2-fe67590a4d6f"],

Cell["\<\
The training target is not one-hot. With \[CurlyEpsilon] = 0.1 and K classes \
it puts 1 \[Minus] \[CurlyEpsilon] + \[CurlyEpsilon]/K on the right class and \
\[CurlyEpsilon]/K on each of the others. The model learns to be less sure; \
the paper reports that this hurts perplexity but improves accuracy and BLEU \
(Section 5.4).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b1a1521c-3d63-4b73-ab51-36c65e3f6e41"],

Cell["q = (1 \[Minus] \[CurlyEpsilon]) onehot(y) + \[CurlyEpsilon]/K ,        \
loss = \[Minus] \[CapitalSigma]\:2096 q\:2096 log p\:2096", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"5cfd60df-ff09-4eed-8743-d80a68d072fd"],

Cell["\<\
K = 4, right class 3, \[CurlyEpsilon] = 0.1: q = (0.025, 0.025, 0.925, \
0.025). If the model predicts q itself the loss is \[Minus](0.925 ln 0.925 + \
3 \[Times] 0.025 ln 0.025) = 0.0721 + 0.2767 = 0.349. If it is 99.9 % sure of \
class 3, the three small classes cost 0.075 \[Times] ln(3/0.001) \
\[TildeTilde] 0.075 \[Times] 8.01 = 0.601, and the total is 0.601: being too \
sure is now penalised.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"2551b8fe-a347-4a97-a29b-1d570d9e4b7b"],

