        (Identity[#]& )[
         Part[#, 2]]}& )}},
  PlotInteractivity:>True,
  PlotLabel->FormBox[
   "\"The loss is lowest at 0.925, not at 1\"", TraditionalForm],
  PlotRange->{{0.3000000142653061, 0.9989999857346938}, {0., 1.2}},
  PlotRangeClipping->True,
  PlotRangePadding->{{
     Scaled[0.02], 
     Scaled[0.02]}, {0, 0}},
  Ticks->{Automatic, Automatic}]], "Output",
 CellLabel->"Out[19]=",ExpressionUUID->"79e37f34-47f2-4f30-8cb6-587593e065ab"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Fig. 5. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11]],
 "The label-smoothed loss for K = 4 as a function of the probability given to \
the right class (the rest shared equally). Its minimum is at 1 \[Minus] \
\[CurlyEpsilon] + \[CurlyEpsilon]/K = 0.925 (dashed)."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d5945b64-4829-4034-9c82-b3cc778a7520"],

Cell["12. The warm-up learning-rate schedule", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"55d60c1d-51eb-4311-b437-301342d634a2"],

Cell["\<\
Adam with \[Beta]\:2081 = 0.9, \[Beta]\:2082 = 0.98, \[CurlyEpsilon] = 10\
\:207b\:2079. The learning rate rises linearly for the first 4000 steps, then \
falls as 1/\[Sqrt]step (Section 5.3). The warm-up protects the young network \
from large, badly aimed steps.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6755d18e-54f0-4314-acac-19aeb8dbc7f1"],

Cell["\<\
lrate = dmodel^(\[Minus]0.5) \[CenterDot] min(step^(\[Minus]0.5), step \
\[CenterDot] warmup^(\[Minus]1.5)),      warmup = 4000\
\>", "Text",
 TextAlignment->Center,
 FontFamily->"Times",
 FontSize->15,
 FontSlant->"Italic",ExpressionUUID->"f0f979c2-e4ff-44d6-bca2-dc7429659dda"],

Cell["\<\
The two terms are equal when step^(\[Minus]0.5) = step \[CenterDot] 4000^(\
\[Minus]1.5), that is at step = 4000. There the rate is 512^(\[Minus]0.5) \
\[Times] 4000^(\[Minus]0.5) = 0.04419 \[Times] 0.01581 = 6.99 \[Times] 10\
\:207b\:2074, the peak.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"4a4d9788-46e1-42b9-9536-3593a52e0da0"],

