Cell["14. How big is the base model?", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e336f74b-f509-4335-a0a6-e2e3cf07accf"],

Cell["\<\
Counted from the parts above, for dmodel = 512, dff = 2048, h = 8, 6 encoder \
and 6 decoder layers and the shared vocabulary of about 37 000 tokens \
(Section 5.1).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"fca54547-47b2-4d9a-99a8-28909df745f1"],

Cell["\<\
Attention: 4(512\.b2 + 512) = 1 050 624. Feed-forward: 512 \[Times] 2048 + \
2048 + 2048 \[Times] 512 + 512 = 2 099 712. LayerNorm: 2 \[Times] 512 = 1024. \
An encoder layer has 1 050 624 + 2 099 712 + 2 \[Times] 1024 = 3 152 384, a \
decoder layer 2 \[Times] 1 050 624 + 2 099 712 + 3 \[Times] 1024 = 4 204 032. \
Six of each: 18 914 304 + 25 224 192 = 44 138 496. The shared embedding adds \
37 000 \[Times] 512 = 18 944 000 and the softmax biases 37 000. Total 63 119 \
496, within 3 % of the 65M of the paper\[CloseCurlyQuote]s Table 3.\
\>", "Text",
 CellFrame->{{3, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.83, 0.34, 0.11],
 Background->RGBColor[
  1, 0.97, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"128c4836-c451-4ed3-98f6-20369b276950"],

